{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Two shoulder-pieces.</b> Like two straps. <b>Joined</b> — this one at the side of that one. <b>It shall have</b> — the ephod <b>at its two ends</b> — the shoulder-pieces shall be for it at each of its two ends, one on the right and one on the left. And because they stand upright and rise up to the priest's shoulders, they are called shoulder-pieces." "<b>Two shoulder-pieces it shall have</b> — the ephod. <b>At its two ends, and joined</b> — he shall join them by means of a needle with weaving, corresponding to the two ends of the ephod, so that they stand upright and rise upon his two shoulders along his back, and therefore they are called shoulder-pieces. And one may say that they are broad, as it is written, ״שתי כתפת חברת״ — for if they were nothing but two straps rising upon his shoulders, when the priest is occupied in the service and bends his shoulders this way and that way, they would separate on both sides and the breastplate would fall." "<b>And joined.</b> The ephod shall be joined by means of a needle to the shoulder-pieces."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:50.876715247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}